 attachment capabilities.\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"I found the current detection script. Next I’m checking how OpenClaw can send media back into Telegram so I can wire this in the right way instead of bolting on a brittle workaround.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0f6fd7f0a916ebe60169bab38a8e048191966ade9a34ca55f2\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_g67pPIVFcKg3Kov29fTzufbX|fc_0f6fd7f0a916ebe60169bab38c5b648191b5c1d365413f4db7","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -RIn \"send.*photo\\|send.*image\\|attachment\\|attachments\\|telegram\" /app/docs /home/node/.openclaw/workspace 2>/dev/null | head -200","workdir":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace","yieldMs":10000},"partialJson":"{\"command\":\"grep -RIn \\\"send.*photo\\\\|send.*image\\\\|attachment\\\\|attachments\\\\|telegram\\\" /app/docs /home/node/.openclaw/workspace 2>/dev/null | head -200\",\"workdir\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace\",\"yieldMs\":10000}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_FF4ee39XMdGzvA72uDYVSTF4|fc_0f6fd7f0a916ebe60169bab38c5b748191a9d2bbb7afb9d6c1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -RIn \"kidney_cancer_tool.py\\|kidney-cancer-detection\" /home/node/.openclaw /app 2>/dev/null | head -200","workdir":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace","yieldMs":10000},"partialJson":"{\"command\":\"grep -RIn \\\"kidney_cancer_tool.py\\\\|kidney-cancer-detection\\\" /home/node/.openclaw /app 2>/dev/null | head -200\",\"workdir\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace\",\"yieldMs\":10000}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":2230,"output":467,"cacheRead":13184,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":15881,"cost":{"input":0.005575,"output":0.007005,"cacheRead":0.003296,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.015876}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1773843324599}}
{"type":"message","id":"ccc87db8","parentId":"e72f7be2","timestamp":"2026-03-18T14:15:40.438Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_g67pPIVFcKg3Kov29fTzufbX|fc_0f6fd7f0a916ebe60169bab38c5b648191b5c1d365413f4db7","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/app/docs/nodes/audio.md:13:  1. Locates the first audio attachment (local path or URL) and downloads it if needed.\n/app/docs/nodes/audio.md:140:- Use `tools.media.audio.attachments` to process multiple voice notes (`mode: \"all\"` + `maxAttachments`).\n/app/docs/nodes/audio.md:175:- Set `channels.telegram.groups.<chatId>.disableAudioPreflight: true` to skip preflight transcript mention checks for that group.\n/app/docs/nodes/audio.md:176:- Set `channels.telegram.groups.<chatId>.topics.<threadId>.disableAudioPreflight` to override per-topic (`true` to skip, `false` to force-enable).\n/app/docs/nodes/audio.md:187:- Preflight transcription only processes the **first** audio attachment for mention detection. Additional audio is processed during the main media understanding phase.\n/app/docs/nodes/images.md:4:  - Modifying media pipeline or attachments\n/app/docs/nodes/images.md:51:- By default only the first matching image/audio/video attachment is processed; set `tools.media.<cap>.attachments` to process multiple attachments.\n/app/docs/nodes/images.md:70:- Cover send + reply flows for image/audio/document cases.\n/app/docs/nodes/camera.md:66:The easiest way to get attachments is via the CLI helper, which writes decoded media to a temp file and prints `MEDIA:<path>`.\n/app/docs/nodes/media-understanding.md:22:1. Collect inbound attachments (`MediaPaths`, `MediaUrls`, `MediaTypes`).\n/app/docs/nodes/media-understanding.md:23:2. For each enabled capability (image/audio/video), select attachments per policy (default: **first**).\n/app/docs/nodes/media-understanding.md:32:If understanding fails or is disabled, **the reply flow continues** with the original body + attachments.\n/app/docs/nodes/media-understanding.md:45:  - `attachments` policy (`mode`, `maxAttachments`, `prefer`)\n/app/docs/nodes/media-understanding.md:212:Per‑capability `attachments` controls which attachments are processed:\n/app/docs/nodes/media-understanding.md:249:        attachments: { mode: \"all\", maxAttachments: 2 },\n/app/docs/nodes/index.md:167:Higher-level helpers exist for the common “give the agent a MEDIA attachment” workflows.\n/app/docs/reference/test.md:13:- `pnpm test:coverage`: Runs the unit suite with V8 coverage (via `vitest.unit.config.ts`). Global thresholds are 70% lines/branches/functions/statements. Coverage excludes integration-heavy entrypoints (CLI wiring, gateway/telegram bridges, webchat static server) to keep the target focused on unit-testable logic.\n/app/docs/reference/wizard.md:90:    - [Telegram](/channels/telegram): bot token.\n/app/docs/reference/wizard.md:297:- `channels.telegram.botToken`, `channels.discord.token`, `channels.signal.*`, `channels.imessage.*`\n/app/docs/reference/wizard.md:319:- Providers: [WhatsApp](/channels/whatsapp), [Telegram](/channels/telegram), [Discord](/channels/discord), [Google Chat](/channels/googlechat), [Signal](/channels/signal), [BlueBubbles](/channels/bluebubbles) (iMessage), [iMessage](/channels/imessage) (legacy)\n/app/docs/reference/secretref-user-supplied-credentials-matrix.json:332:      \"id\": \"channels.telegram.accounts.*.botToken\",\n/app/docs/reference/secretref-user-supplied-credentials-matrix.json:334:      \"path\": \"channels.telegram.accounts.*.botToken\",\n/app/docs/reference/secretref-user-supplied-credentials-matrix.json:339:      \"id\": \"channels.telegram.accounts.*.webhookSecret\",\n/app/docs/reference/secretref-user-supplied-credentials-matrix.json:341:      \"path\": \"channels.telegram.accounts.*.webhookSecret\",\n/app/docs/reference/secretref-user-supplied-credentials-matrix.json:346:      \"id\": \"channels.telegram.botToken\",\n/app/docs/reference/secretref-user-supplied-credentials-matrix.json:348:      \"path\": \"channels.telegram.botToken\",\n/app/docs/reference/secretref-user-supplied-credentials-matrix.json:353:      \"id\": \"channels.telegram.webhookSecret\",\n/app/docs/reference/secretref-user-supplied-credentials-matrix.json:355:      \"path\": \"channels.telegram.webhookSecret\",\n/app/docs/reference/secretref-credential-surface.md:45:- `channels.telegram.botToken`\n/app/docs/reference/secretref-credential-surface.md:46:- `channels.telegram.webhookSecret`\n/app/docs/reference/secretref-credential-surface.md:47:- `channels.telegram.accounts.*.botToken`\n/app/docs/reference/secretref-credential-surface.md:48:- `channels.telegram.accounts.*.webhookSecret`\n/app/docs/docs.json:144:      \"destination\": \"/channels/telegram\"\n/app/docs/docs.json:175:      \"source\": \"/providers/telegram\",\n/app/docs/docs.json:176:      \"destination\": \"/channels/telegram\"\n/app/docs/docs.json:372:      \"destination\": \"/channels/telegram\"\n/app/docs/docs.json:376:      \"destination\": \"/channels/telegram\"\n/app/docs/docs.json:647:      \"source\": \"/telegram\",\n/app/docs/docs.json:648:      \"destination\": \"/channels/telegram\"\n/app/docs/docs.json:921:                  \"channels/telegram\",\n/app/docs/docs.json:1520:                  \"zh-CN/channels/telegram\",\n/app/docs/providers/deepgram.md:4:  - You want Deepgram speech-to-text for audio attachments\n/app/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:253:- `delivery.channel`: `whatsapp` / `telegram` / `discord` / `slack` / `mattermost` (plugin) / `signal` / `imessage` / `last`.\n/app/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:277:Prefixed targets like `telegram:...` / `telegram:group:...` are also accepted:\n/app/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:279:- `telegram:group:-1001234567890:topic:123`\n/app/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:587:  --channel telegram \\\n/app/docs/automation/cron-jobs.md:678:- If you see `telegram:...` prefixes in logs or stored “last route” targets, that’s normal;\n/app/docs/automation/webhook.md:86:- `channel` optional (string): The messaging channel for delivery. One of: `last`, `whatsapp`, `telegram`, `discord`, `slack`, `mattermost` (plugin), `signal`, `imessage`, `msteams`. Defaults to `last`.\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:225:    commandSource?: string,    // e.g., 'whatsapp', 'telegram'\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:274:- **`message:received`**: When an inbound message is received from any channel. Fires early in processing before media understanding. Content may contain raw placeholders like `<media:audio>` for media attachments that haven't been processed yet.\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:289:  channelId: string,      // Channel (e.g., \"whatsapp\", \"telegram\", \"discord\")\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:311:  channelId: string,      // Channel (e.g., \"whatsapp\", \"telegram\", \"discord\")\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:324:  channelId: string,      // Channel (e.g., \"telegram\", \"whatsapp\")\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:334:  channelId: string,      // Channel (e.g., \"telegram\", \"whatsapp\")\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:596:- **Source**: telegram\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:671:{\"timestamp\":\"2026-01-16T14:30:00.000Z\",\"action\":\"new\",\"sessionKey\":\"agent:main:main\",\"senderId\":\"+1234567890\",\"source\":\"telegram\"}\n/app/docs/automation/poll.md:22:openclaw message poll --channel telegram --target 123456789 \\\n/app/docs/automation/poll.md:24:openclaw message poll --channel telegram --target -1001234567890:topic:42 \\\n/app/docs/automation/poll.md:47:- `--channel`: `whatsapp` (default), `telegram`, `discord`, or `msteams`\n/app/docs/channels/zalo.md:137:- **Image messages**: Download and process inbound images; send images via `sendPhoto`.\n/app/docs/channels/matrix.md:141:Multi-account support: use `channels.matrix.accounts` with per-account credentials and optional `name`. See [`gateway/configuration`](/gateway/configuration#telegramaccounts--discordaccounts--slackaccounts--signalaccounts--imessageaccounts) for the shared pattern.\n/app/docs/channels/slack.md:259:  <Accordion title=\"Inbound attachments\">\n/app/docs/channels/slack.md:260:    Slack file attachments are downloaded from Slack-hosted private URLs (token-authenticated request flow) and written to the media store when fetch succeeds and size limits permit.\n/app/docs/channels/imessage.md:90:    Recommended config when attachments are enabled:\n/app/docs/channels/imessage.md:98:      remoteHost: \"user@gateway-host\", // used for SCP attachment fetches\n/app/docs/channels/imessage.md:100:      // Optional: override allowed attachment roots.\n/app/docs/channels/imessage.md:102:      attachmentRoots: [\"/Users/*/Library/Messages/Attachments\"],\n/app/docs/channels/imessage.md:112:    Attachment paths are validated against allowed roots (`attachmentRoots` / `remoteAttachmentRoots`).\n/app/docs/channels/imessage.md:211:    - `remoteHost` enables SCP attachment fetches\n/app/docs/channels/imessage.md:242:    Each account can override fields such as `cliPath`, `dbPath`, `allowFrom`, `groupPolicy`, `mediaMaxMb`, history settings, and attachment root allowlists.\n/app/docs/channels/imessage.md:251:    - inbound attachment ingestion is optional: `channels.imessage.includeAttachments`\n/app/docs/channels/imessage.md:252:    - remote attachment paths can be fetched via SCP when `remoteHost` is set\n/app/docs/channels/imessage.md:253:    - attachment paths must match allowed roots:\n/app/docs/channels/imessage.md:254:      - `channels.imessage.attachmentRoots` (local)\n/app/docs/channels/imessage.md:338:  <Accordion title=\"Remote attachments fail\">\n/app/docs/channels/discord.md:303:File attachments:\n/app/docs/channels/discord.md:305:- `file` blocks must point to an attachment reference (`attachment://<filename>`)\n/app/docs/channels/discord.md:306:- Provide the attachment via `media`/`path`/`filePath` (single file); use `media-gallery` for multiple files\n/app/docs/channels/discord.md:307:- Use `filename` to override the upload name when it should match the attachment reference\n/app/docs/channels/discord.md:1008:OpenClaw can join Discord voice channels for realtime, continuous conversations. This is separate from voice message attachments.\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:39:    telegram: {\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:50:    Telegram does **not** use `openclaw channels login telegram`; configure token in config/env, then start gateway.\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:58:openclaw pairing list telegram\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:59:openclaw pairing approve telegram <CODE>\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:67:    Add the bot to your group, then set `channels.telegram.groups` and `groupPolicy` to match your access model.\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:109:    `channels.telegram.dmPolicy` controls direct message access:\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:116:    `channels.telegram.allowFrom` accepts numeric Telegram user IDs. `telegram:` / `tg:` prefixes are accepted and normalized.\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:120:    If you previously relied on pairing-store allowlist files, `openclaw doctor --fix` can recover entries into `channels.telegram.allowFrom` in allowlist flows (for example when `dmPolicy: \"allowlist\"` has no explicit IDs yet).\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:135:curl \"https://api.telegram.org/bot<bot_token>/getUpdates\"\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:145:    1. **Which groups are allowed** (`channels.telegram.groups`)\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:151:    2. **Which senders are allowed in groups** (`channels.telegram.groupPolicy`)\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:157:    `groupAllowFrom` entries should be numeric Telegram user IDs (`telegram:` / `tg:` prefixes are normalized).\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:158:    Do not put Telegram group or supergroup chat IDs in `groupAllowFrom`. Negative chat IDs belong under `channels.telegram.groups`.\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:162:    Runtime note: if `channels.telegram` is completely missing, runtime defaults to fail-closed `groupPolicy=\"allowlist\"` unless `channels.defaults.groupPolicy` is explicitly set.\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:169:    telegram: {\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:186:    telegram: {\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:201:      - Put negative Telegram group or supergroup chat IDs like `-1001234567890` under `channels.telegram.groups`.\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:230:    telegram: {\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:269:    - `channels.telegram.streaming` is `off | partial | block | progress` (default: `partial`)\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:271:    - legacy `channels.telegram.streamMode` and boolean `streaming` values are auto-mapped\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:298:    Link previews are enabled by default and can be disabled with `channels.telegram.linkPreview: false`.\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:314:    telegram: {\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:340:    - `setMyCommands failed` with `BOT_COMMANDS_TOO_MUCH` means the Telegram menu still overflowed after trimming; reduce plugin/skill/custom commands or disable `channels.telegram.commands.native`.\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:341:    - `setMyCommands failed` with network/fetch errors usually means outbound DNS/HTTPS to `api.telegram.org` is blocked.\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:351:    More details: [Pairing](/channels/pairing#pair-via-telegram-recommended-for-ios).\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:361:    telegram: {\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:375:    telegram: {\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:403:  channel: \"telegram\",\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:434:    - `channels.telegram.actions.sendMessage`\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:435:    - `channels.telegram.actions.deleteMessage`\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:436:    - `channels.telegram.actions.reactions`\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:437:    - `channels.telegram.actions.sticker` (default: disabled)\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:439:    Note: `edit` and `topic-create` are currently enabled by default and do not have separate `channels.telegram.actions.*` toggles.\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:452:    `channels.telegram.replyToMode` controls handling:\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:468:      `channels.telegram.groups.<chatId>.topics.<threadId>`\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:483:        telegram: {\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:498:    Each topic then has its own session key: `agent:zu:telegram:group:-1001234567890:topic:3`\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:502:    - `bindings[]` with `type: \"acp\"` and `match.channel: \"telegram\"`\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:529:            channel: \"telegram\",\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:536:        telegram: {\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:558:    - Requires `channels.telegram.threadBindings.spawnAcpSessions=true`.\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:584:  channel: \"telegram\",\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:600:  channel: \"telegram\",\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:627:    - `~/.openclaw/telegram/sticker-cache.json`\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:636:    telegram: {\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:650:  channel: \"telegram\",\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:661:  channel: \"telegram\",\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:678:    - `channels.telegram.reactionNotifications`: `off | own | all` (default: `own`)\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:679:    - `channels.telegram.reactionLevel`: `off | ack | minimal | extensive` (default: `minimal`)\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:698:    - `channels.telegram.accounts.<accountId>.ackReaction`\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:699:    - `channels.telegram.ackReaction`\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:715:    - group migration events (`migrate_to_chat_id`) to update `channels.telegram.groups`\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:723:    telegram: {\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:737:    - set `channels.telegram.webhookUrl`\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:738:    - set `channels.telegram.webhookSecret` (required when webhook URL is set)\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:739:    - optional `channels.telegram.webhookPath` (default `/telegram-webhook`)\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:740:    - optional `channels.telegram.webhookHost` (default `127.0.0.1`)\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:741:    - optional `channels.telegram.webhookPort` (default `8787`)\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:751:    - `channels.telegram.textChunkLimit` default is 4000.\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:752:    - `channels.telegram.chunkMode=\"newline\"` prefers paragraph boundaries (blank lines) before length splitting.\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:753:    - `channels.telegram.mediaMaxMb` (default 100) caps inbound and outbound Telegram media size.\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:754:    - `channels.telegram.timeoutSeconds` overrides Telegram API client timeout (if unset, grammY default applies).\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:755:    - group context history uses `channels.telegram.historyLimit` or `messages.groupChat.historyLimit` (default 50); `0` disables.\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:757:      - `channels.telegram.dmHistoryLimit`\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:758:      - `channels.telegram.dms[\"<user_id>\"].historyLimit`\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:759:    - `channels.telegram.retry` config applies to Telegram send helpers (CLI/tools/actions) for recoverable outbound API errors.\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:764:openclaw message send --channel telegram --target 123456789 --message \"hi\"\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:765:openclaw message send --channel telegram --target @name --message \"hi\"\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:771:openclaw message poll --channel telegram --target 123456789 \\\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:773:openclaw message poll --channel telegram --target -1001234567890:topic:42 \\\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:787:    - `channels.telegram.actions.sendMessage=false` disables outbound Telegram messages, including polls\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:788:    - `channels.telegram.actions.poll=false` disables Telegram poll creation while leaving regular sends enabled\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:797:    - `channels.telegram.execApprovals.enabled`\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:798:    - `channels.telegram.execApprovals.approvers`\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:799:    - `channels.telegram.execApprovals.target` (`dm` | `channel` | `both`, default: `dm`)\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:814:    Inline approval buttons also depend on `channels.telegram.capabilities.inlineButtons` allowing the target surface (`dm`, `group`, or `all`).\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:837:    - when `channels.telegram.groups` exists, group must be listed (or include `\"*\"`)\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:848:    - `setMyCommands failed` with network/fetch errors usually indicates DNS/HTTPS reachability issues to `api.telegram.org`\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:855:    - Some hosts resolve `api.telegram.org` to IPv6 first; broken IPv6 egress can cause intermittent Telegram API failures.\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:857:    - On VPS hosts with unstable direct egress/TLS, route Telegram API calls through `channels.telegram.proxy`:\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:861:  telegram:\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:870:  telegram:\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:882:dig +short api.telegram.org A\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:883:dig +short api.telegram.org AAAA\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:895:- `channels.telegram.enabled`: enable/disable channel startup.\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:896:- `channels.telegram.botToken`: bot token (BotFather).\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:897:- `channels.telegram.tokenFile`: read token from a regular file path. Symlinks are rejected.\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:898:- `channels.telegram.dmPolicy`: `pairing | allowlist | open | disabled` (default: pairing).\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:899:- `channels.telegram.allowFrom`: DM allowlist (numeric Telegram user IDs). `allowlist` requires at least one sender ID. `open` requires `\"*\"`. `openclaw doctor --fix` can resolve legacy `@username` entries to IDs and can recover allowlist entries from pairing-store files in allowlist migration flows.\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:900:- `channels.telegram.actions.poll`: enable or disable Telegram poll creation (default: enabled; still requires `sendMessage`).\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:901:- `channels.telegram.defaultTo`: default Telegram target used by CLI `--deliver` when no explicit `--reply-to` is provided.\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:902:- `channels.telegram.groupPolicy`: `open | allowlist | disabled` (default: allowlist).\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:903:- `channels.telegram.groupAllowFrom`: group sender allowlist (numeric Telegram user IDs). `openclaw doctor --fix` can resolve legacy `@username` entries to IDs. Non-numeric entries are ignored at auth time. Group auth does not use DM pairing-store fallback (`2026.2.25+`).\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:905:  - When two or more account IDs are configured, set `channels.telegram.defaultAccount` (or include `channels.telegram.accounts.default`) to make default routing explicit.\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:907:  - `channels.telegram.accounts.default.allowFrom` and `channels.telegram.accounts.default.groupAllowFrom` apply only to the `default` account.\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:908:  - Named accounts inherit `channels.telegram.allowFrom` and `channels.telegram.groupAllowFrom` when account-level values are unset.\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:909:  - Named accounts do not inherit `channels.telegram.accounts.default.allowFrom` / `groupAllowFrom`.\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:910:- `channels.telegram.groups`: per-group defaults + allowlist (use `\"*\"` for global defaults).\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:911:  - `channels.telegram.groups.<id>.groupPolicy`: per-group override for groupPolicy (`open | allowlist | disabled`).\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:912:  - `channels.telegram.groups.<id>.requireMention`: mention gating default.\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:913:  - `channels.telegram.groups.<id>.skills`: skill filter (omit = all skills, empty = none).\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:914:  - `channels.telegram.groups.<id>.allowFrom`: per-group sender allowlist override.\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:915:  - `channels.telegram.groups.<id>.systemPrompt`: extra system prompt for the group.\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:916:  - `channels.telegram.groups.<id>.enabled`: disable the group when `false`.\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:917:  - `channels.telegram.groups.<id>.topics.<threadId>.*`: per-topic overrides (group fields + topic-only `agentId`).\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:918:  - `channels.telegram.groups.<id>.topics.<threadId>.agentId`: route this topic to a specific agent (overrides group-level and binding routing).\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:919:- `channels.telegram.groups.<id>.topics.<threadId>.groupPolicy`: per-topic override for groupPolicy (`open | allowlist | disabled`).\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:920:- `channels.telegram.groups.<id>.topics.<threadId>.requireMention`: per-topic mention gating override.\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:922:- `channels.telegram.direct.<id>.topics.<threadId>.agentId`: route DM topics to a specific agent (same behavior as forum topics).\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:923:- `channels.telegram.execApprovals.enabled`: enable Telegram as a chat-based exec approval client for this account.\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:924:- `channels.telegram.execApprovals.approvers`: Telegram user IDs allowed to approve or deny exec requests. Required when exec approvals are enabled.\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:925:- `channels.telegram.execApprovals.target`: `dm | channel | both` (default: `dm`). `channel` and `both` preserve the originating Telegram topic when present.\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:926:- `channels.telegram.execApprovals.agentFilter`: optional agent ID filter for forwarded approval prompts.\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:927:- `channels.telegram.execApprovals.sessionFilter`: optional session key filter (substring or regex) for forwarded approval prompts.\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:928:- `channels.telegram.accounts.<account>.execApprovals`: per-account override for Telegram exec approval routing and approver authorization.\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:929:- `channels.telegram.capabilities.inlineButtons`: `off | dm | group | all | allowlist` (default: allowlist).\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:930:- `channels.telegram.accounts.<account>.capabilities.inlineButtons`: per-account override.\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:931:- `channels.telegram.commands.nativeSkills`: enable/disable Telegram native skills commands.\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:932:- `channels.telegram.replyToMode`: `off | first | all` (default: `off`).\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:933:- `channels.telegram.textChunkLimit`: outbound chunk size (chars)."}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":19,"aggregated":"/app/docs/nodes/audio.md:13:  1. Locates the first audio attachment (local path or URL) and downloads it if needed.\n/app/docs/nodes/audio.md:140:- Use `tools.media.audio.attachments` to process multiple voice notes (`mode: \"all\"` + `maxAttachments`).\n/app/docs/nodes/audio.md:175:- Set `channels.telegram.groups.<chatId>.disableAudioPreflight: true` to skip preflight transcript mention checks for that group.\n/app/docs/nodes/audio.md:176:- Set `channels.telegram.groups.<chatId>.topics.<threadId>.disableAudioPreflight` to override per-topic (`true` to skip, `false` to force-enable).\n/app/docs/nodes/audio.md:187:- Preflight transcription only processes the **first** audio attachment for mention detection. Additional audio is processed during the main media understanding phase.\n/app/docs/nodes/images.md:4:  - Modifying media pipeline or attachments\n/app/docs/nodes/images.md:51:- By default only the first matching image/audio/video attachment is processed; set `tools.media.<cap>.attachments` to process multiple attachments.\n/app/docs/nodes/images.md:70:- Cover send + reply flows for image/audio/document cases.\n/app/docs/nodes/camera.md:66:The easiest way to get attachments is via the CLI helper, which writes decoded media to a temp file and prints `MEDIA:<path>`.\n/app/docs/nodes/media-understanding.md:22:1. Collect inbound attachments (`MediaPaths`, `MediaUrls`, `MediaTypes`).\n/app/docs/nodes/media-understanding.md:23:2. For each enabled capability (image/audio/video), select attachments per policy (default: **first**).\n/app/docs/nodes/media-understanding.md:32:If understanding fails or is disabled, **the reply flow continues** with the original body + attachments.\n/app/docs/nodes/media-understanding.md:45:  - `attachments` policy (`mode`, `maxAttachments`, `prefer`)\n/app/docs/nodes/media-understanding.md:212:Per‑capability `attachments` controls which attachments are processed:\n/app/docs/nodes/media-understanding.md:249:        attachments: { mode: \"all\", maxAttachments: 2 },\n/app/docs/nodes/index.md:167:Higher-level helpers exist for the common “give the agent a MEDIA attachment” workflows.\n/app/docs/reference/test.md:13:- `pnpm test:coverage`: Runs the unit suite with V8 coverage (via `vitest.unit.config.ts`). Global thresholds are 70% lines/branches/functions/statements. Coverage excludes integration-heavy entrypoints (CLI wiring, gateway/telegram bridges, webchat static server) to keep the target focused on unit-testable logic.\n/app/docs/reference/wizard.md:90:    - [Telegram](/channels/telegram): bot token.\n/app/docs/reference/wizard.md:297:- `channels.telegram.botToken`, `channels.discord.token`, `channels.signal.*`, `channels.imessage.*`\n/app/docs/reference/wizard.md:319:- Providers: [WhatsApp](/channels/whatsapp), [Telegram](/channels/telegram), [Discord](/channels/discord), [Google Chat](/channels/googlechat), [Signal](/channels/signal), [BlueBubbles](/channels/bluebubbles) (iMessage), [iMessage](/channels/imessage) (legacy)\n/app/docs/reference/secretref-user-supplied-credential