gopfPWgYojCNYA44_GxQ4vl7JatY8kN9nKEtscAaYiQOBRnqsrhENUjiWD5v-o7ouCsnwtnBoRnCNY-foAkAjvchGeM2Y93PinV2vGz9Y60ZGy-sg_sy1eyw==\\\",\\\"summary\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"summary_text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"**Considering git repo options**\\\\n\\\\nIt seems I need to mention that I couldn’t commit because there’s no git repository. I’m wondering if maybe the git repo is located elsewhere, but I’m not sure about that either. Could I even initialize a new repository here? No, that doesn’t seem right either. I just want to finalize this in a concise way, but the situation is a bit tangled, and I need to sort it out.\\\"}]}\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"[[reply_to_current]] Done.\\n\\nWhat I changed:\\n- Removed the static image-path behavior from `~/.openclaw/skills/kidney-cancer-detector/scripts/kidney_cancer_tool.py`.\\n- Added an upload step that:\\n  - sends the local image as `POST multipart/form-data`\\n  - keeps `storage_ref=nodes_bucket` and `local_file_path=upload/` fixed\\n  - replaces `user_id` with the provided Telegram user ID\\n- Reads the upload response and builds the new inference `image_path` as `path + filename`.\\n- Uses that uploaded `image_path` for the kidney cancer detection request.\\n- Updated `SKILL.md` to document the new workflow and usage.\\n\\nNew usage:\\n```bash\\npython3 scripts/kidney_cancer_tool.py --telegram-user-id <telegram-user-id> [local-image-path]\\n```\\n\\nNotes:\\n- If `local-image-path` is omitted, the script now tries to use the newest supported image from `./config/media/inbound`.\\n- I also cleaned up the skill frontmatter so it matches the expected skill format.\\n- I validated the script locally with `py_compile` and `--help`.\\n\\nOne caveat:\\n- I could not create a git commit because `/home/node/.openclaw/workspace` is not a git repository in this environment.\\n\\nIf you want, I can also make the script automatically pull the Telegram user ID from message/session metadata instead of requiring `--telegram-user-id`/`TELEGRAM_USER_ID`.\",\"textSignature\":\"{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"id\\\":\\\"msg_0a43ffedc4cd476a0169b7d5afc6788191816a512b3d4309cb\\\",\\\"phase\\\":\\\"final_answer\\\"}\"}],\"api\":\"openai-codex-responses\",\"provider\":\"openai-codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.4\",\"usage\":{\"input\":135,\"output\":345,\"cacheRead\":18560,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"totalTokens\":19040,\"cost\":{\"input\":0.0003375,\"output\":0.005175,\"cacheRead\":0.00464,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"total\":0.0101525}},\"stopReason\":\"stop\",\"timestamp\":1773655462009}}\n/home/node/.openclaw/agents/main/sessions/e76bd25e-909a-4706-a6c1-45bbcb6c44a8.jsonl.reset.2026-03-18T13-39-11.126Z:9:{\"type\":\"message\",\"id\":\"f44dff16\",\"parentId\":\"086ed3c8\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-03-18T13:35:08.193Z\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"toolResult\",\"toolCallId\":\"call_L5vsB4CRiJPuwiHZdD9Xmnjl|fc_0801a12b6226b3690169baaa0bfd1481918df23a37cc426aea\",\"toolName\":\"read\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"---\\nname: kidney-cancer-detection\\ndescription: Use this skill when the user wants to analyze a kidney medical image for possible kidney cancer detection, classify the result, or route a kidney image through the upload API and then into the kidney cancer prediction endpoint using the returned remote image path.\\n---\\n\\n# Kidney Cancer Detection\\n\\nUpload the local image first, then run inference with the uploaded remote path.\\n\\n## Workflow\\n\\n1. Determine the local image to analyze.\\n   - Prefer an explicit local file path when one is available.\\n   - If no path is provided, use the most recent supported image under `./config/media/inbound`.\\n2. Require the Telegram user id.\\n   - Pass it as `--telegram-user-id` or set `TELEGRAM_USER_ID`.\\n   - Use that value as the upload request's `user_id` query parameter.\\n3. Upload the image with a `POST multipart/form-data` request to:\\n   - `http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/nodes/input/upload?storage_ref=nodes_bucket&local_file_path=upload%2F&user_id=<telegram-user-id>`\\n4. Read the upload response JSON and build the new remote `image_path` by concatenating:\\n   - `path + filename`\\n5. Call the kidney cancer inference endpoint using that uploaded `image_path`.\\n\\n## Fixed request values\\n\\nKeep these values static:\\n- `storage_ref`: `nodes_bucket`\\n- `local_file_path`: `upload/`\\n- inference endpoint `data.storage_ref`: `nodes_bucket`\\n\\n## What this skill runs\\n\\n```bash\\npython3 scripts/kidney_cancer_tool.py --telegram-user-id <telegram-user-id> [local-image-path]\\n```\\n\\nIf `local-image-path` is omitted, the script automatically selects the newest supported image from `./config/media/inbound`.\\n\\n## Upload response handling\\n\\nGiven an upload response like:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"path\\\": \\\"upload/2026-03-15_14.52.42_5EdSbYnzCrKdhainPvGx/\\\",\\n  \\\"filename\\\": \\\"9dd106ff-65ad-4a16-a381-6d76e4845c9c.jpg\\\",\\n  \\\"column_names\\\": null\\n}\\n```\\n\\nBuild:\\n\\n```text\\nimage_path = \\\"upload/2026-03-15_14.52.42_5EdSbYnzCrKdhainPvGx/9dd106ff-65ad-4a16-a381-6d76e4845c9c.jpg\\\"\\n```\\n\\nUse that full value as the inference request's `data.image_path`.\\n\\n## Expected output\\n\\nReturn validated JSON with this shape:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"uploaded_image_path\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n  \\\"prediction_label\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n  \\\"confidence\\\": 0.98\\n}\\n```\\n\"}],\"isError\":false,\"timestamp\":1773840908187}}\n/home/node/.openclaw/agents/main/sessions/e76bd25e-909a-4706-a6c1-45bbcb6c44a8.jsonl.reset.2026-03-18T13-39-11.126Z:10:{\"type\":\"message\",\"id\":\"2f969c5d\",\"parentId\":\"f44dff16\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-03-18T13:35:10.521Z\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"\",\"thinkingSignature\":\"{\\\"id\\\":\\\"rs_0801a12b6226b3690169baaa0dbca081919109fb9c8f0ac08c\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"reasoning\\\",\\\"encrypted_content\\\":\\\"gAAAAABpuqoOv-ahdcq4pAV3go4pTQUC1jU3LZ5I6vhhTjlsQhtAWs310lRv0l1V7Ex3vhllhiREWGGS3NTopsTUrxR84NprAPDIpG2T